          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            Passing from a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            to its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf"} presheaf
            category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi PSh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mi op
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Set
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PSh(C) := [C^{op},Set]
            may be regarded as the operation of “freely adjoining
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimits"} colimits
            to
            = succeed "\u201D." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
          %p
            A slightly more precise version of this statement is that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+embedding"} Yoneda embedding
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                  %mo :
                  %mi C
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi PSh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Y : C \hookrightarrow PSh(C)
          %p
            is the
            %strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+construction"} free
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocomplete+category"} cocompletion
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+property"} universal property
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+embedding"} Yoneda embedding
            is expressed in terms of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+extension"} Yoneda extension
            of any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo :
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F : C \to D
            to a category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            with colimits.
          %p
            There is also an alternative construction of the free cocomplete category, given by the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+strict+cocompletion"} free strict cocompletion
          %h2#technical_details Technical details
          %p
            The rough statement is that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+embedding"} Yoneda embedding
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi y
                    %mi S
                  %mo :
                  %mi S
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi Set
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi S
                        %mi op
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y_S: S \to Set^{S^{op}}
          %p
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+category"} small category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            into the category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Set
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi S
                        %mi op
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set^{S^{op}}
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf"} presheaves
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            is universal among functors from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            into
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocomplete+category"} cocomplete categories
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category"} 2-categorical
            sense: given a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo :
                  %mi S
                  %mo →
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F: S \to D
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            is (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+colimit"}> small
            \-)cocomplete, there exists a unique (up to
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocontinuous+functor"} cocontinuous
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extension"} extension
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi Set
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi S
                        %mi op
                  %mo →
                  %mi D
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat{F}: Set^{S^{op}} \to D,
          %p
            called the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+extension"} Yoneda extension
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %msub
                    %mi y
                    %mi S
                  %mo ≅
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat{F} y_S \cong F
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat{F}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/preserved+limit"} preserves
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+colimits"} small colimits
          %p
            Put slightly differently: let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Cocomp
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cocomp
            denote the 2-category of cocomplete categories, cocontinuous functors, and natural transformations between them. Then for cocomplete
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi y
                  %mi S
                  %mo :
                  %mi S
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi Set
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi S
                        %mi op
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y S: S \to Set^{S^{op}}
            induces by restriction a functor
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi res
                    %mrow
                      %mi y
                      %mi S
                  %mi D
                  %mo :
                  %mi Cocomp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi Set
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi S
                        %mi op
                  %mo ,
                  %mi D
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi Cat
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %mo ,
                  %mi D
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} res_{y S} D: Cocomp(Set^{S^{op}}, D) \to Cat(S, D)
          %p
            that is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalence
            for each
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-natural+transformation"} 2-natural
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo ↦
                  %mover
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \mapsto \hat{F}
            gives a functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ext
                    %mrow
                      %mi y
                      %mi S
                  %mi D
                  %mo :
                  %mi Cat
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %mo ,
                  %mi D
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi Cocomp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi Set
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi S
                        %mi op
                  %mo ,
                  %mi D
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ext_{y S}D: Cat(S, D) \to Cocomp(Set^{S^{op}}, D)
            that is a left adjoint to
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi res
                      %mrow
                        %mi y
                        %mi S
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} res_{y S}D
          %p
            As a first step, we construct the desired extension
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat{F}
            as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functor"} left adjoint
            to the functor
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi Set
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi S
                        %mi op
                  %mo :
                  %mi d
                  %mo ↦
                  %msub
                    %mi hom
                    %mi D
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi F
                  %mo −
                  %mo ,
                  %mi d
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D \to Set^{S^{op}}: d \mapsto \hom_D(F-, d).
          %p
            Being a left adjoint,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat{F}
            is cocontinuous.
          %p
            An explicit formula for the left adjoint is given by the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weighted+colimit"} weighted colimit
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/end"} coend
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product+of+functors"} tensor product of functors
            formula
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi X
                  %msub
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi S
                  %mi F
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mo ∫
                    %mrow
                      %mi s
                      %mo :
                      %mi S
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi s
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⋅
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi s
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat{F}(X) = X \otimes_S F = \int^{s: S} X(s) \cdot F(s)
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mo ⋅
                  %mi d
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \cdot d
            is notation for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/power"} copowering
            (or tensoring) an object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            by a set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            (in this case, a coproduct of an
            = succeed "-indexed" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nerve"} nerve
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Day+convolution"} Day convolution
          %p
            This “free cocompletion” property generalizes to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category"} enriched category
            theory. If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            is complete, cocomplete, symmetric monoidal closed, and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            is a small
            = succeed "-enriched" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi V
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi S
                        %mi op
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V^{S^{op}}
            is a free
            = succeed "-cocompletion" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                    %mo =
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V = Set
            = succeed "-enriched" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            = succeed "-cocontinuous" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is not small, then its free cocompletion still exists, but it is not the category of all presheaves on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+presheaves"} small presheaves
            on
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
          %h3#proofs Proofs
          #FreeCocompletion.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+category"} small category
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+embedding"} Yoneda embedding
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mover
                      %mo ↪
                      %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C} \overset{y}{\hookrightarrow} [\mathcal{C}^{op}, Set]
              exhibits the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+presheaves"} category of presheaves
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\mathcal{C}^{op}, Set]
              as the
              %em free co-completion
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+morphism"} universal morphism
              (as in
              %a{:href => "adjoint+functor#UniversalArrow"} this Def.
              but “up to natural isomorphism”) into a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocomplete+category"} cocomplete category
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  for
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝒟
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{D}
                  any
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocomplete+category"} cocomplete category
              %li
                %p
                  for
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi F
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mi 𝒞
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mi 𝒟
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \;\colon\; \mathcal{C} \longrightarrow \mathcal{D}
                  any
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            %p
              there is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mover
                        %mi F
                        %mo ˜
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msup
                        %mi 𝒞
                        %mi op
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Set
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mi 𝒟
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widetilde F \;\colon\; [\mathcal{C}^{op}, Set] \longrightarrow \mathcal{D}
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+isomorphism"} natural isomorphism
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mover
                          %mi F
                          %mo ˜
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widetilde F
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/preserved+limit"} preserves
                  all
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimits"} colimits
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mover
                          %mi F
                          %mo ˜
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widetilde F
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extension"} extends
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi F
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
                  through the
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+embedding"} Yoneda embedding
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+diagram"} diagram commutes
                  = succeed ":" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+isomorphism"} natural isomorphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi 𝒞
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mi y
                            %mo ↙
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⇙
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo ↘
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi F
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                              %mrow
                                %mspace{:width => "negativethinmathspace"}
                                %mspace{:width => "negativethinmathspace"}
                                %mspace{:width => "negativethinmathspace"}
                                %mspace{:width => "negativethinmathspace"}
                                %mspace{:width => "negativethinmathspace"}
                                %mspace{:width => "negativethinmathspace"}
                                %mspace{:width => "negativethinmathspace"}
                                %mspace{:width => "negativethinmathspace"}
                                %mspace{:width => "negativethinmathspace"}
                                %mspace{:width => "negativethinmathspace"}
                                %mspace{:width => "negativethinmathspace"}
                                %mspace{:width => "negativethinmathspace"}
                                %mspace{:width => "negativethinmathspace"}
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                                %msup
                                  %mi 𝒞
                                  %mi op
                                %mo ,
                                %mi Set
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mover
                                %mi F
                                %mo ˜
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi 𝒟
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \&amp;&amp; \mathcal{C}
                    \\\
                    \&amp; {}^{y}\swarrow &amp;\swArrow&amp; \searrow^{\mathrlap{F}}
                    \\\
                    \\mathrlap{ \!\!\!\!\!\!\!\!\!\!\!\!\! [\mathcal{C}^{op}, Set] }
                    \&amp;&amp; \underset{ \widetilde F }{\longrightarrow} &amp;&amp;
                    \\mathcal{D}
                    }
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              The last condition says that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi F
                      %mo ˜
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widetilde F
              is fixed on
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representable+presheaves"} representable presheaves
            #eq:YonedaRestriction.maruku-equation
              %span.maruku-eq-number (1)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi F
                      %mo ˜
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\widetilde F( y(c) ) \simeq F(c)
            %p
              and in fact
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+isomorphism"} naturally
              so:
            #eq:FunctorialYonedaRestriction.maruku-equation
              %span.maruku-eq-number (2)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi c
                              %mn 1
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mi F
                              %mo ˜
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi y
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi c
                              %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≃
                          %mtd
                            %mi F
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi c
                              %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mi f
                            %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mi F
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %mi y
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %mi f
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mi F
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %mi f
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi c
                              %mn 2
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mi F
                              %mo ˜
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi y
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi c
                              %mn 2
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≃
                          %mtd
                            %mi F
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi c
                              %mn 2
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    c_1&amp;&amp;
                    \\widetilde F( y(c_1) ) &amp;\simeq&amp; F(c_1)
                    \\\
                    {}^{\mathllap{f}}\big\downarrow
                    \&amp;&amp; {}^{\mathllap{ F(y(f)) }}\big\downarrow &amp;&amp; \big\downarrow^{\mathrlap{ F(f) }}
                    \\\
                    c_2 &amp;&amp; \widetilde F (y(c_2)) &amp;\simeq&amp; F(c_2)
                    }
            %p
              But the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/co-Yoneda+lemma"} co-Yoneda lemma
              expresses every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf"} presheaf
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi X
                    %mo ∈
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{X} \in [\mathcal{C}^{op}, Set]
              as a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimit
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representable+presheaves"} representable presheaves
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi X
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≃
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msup
                      %mo ∫
                      %mrow
                        %mi c
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi 𝒞
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbf{X} \;\simeq\; \int^{c \in \mathcal{C}} y(c) \cdot \mathbf{X}(c)
                    \\,.
            %p
              Since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde F
              is required to preserve any colimit and hence these particular colimits,
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:YonedaRestriction"} (1)
              implies that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi F
                      %mo ˜
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widetilde F
              is fixed to act, up to isomorphism, as
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mi F
                              %mo ˜
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mover
                              %mi F
                              %mo ˜
                            %mrow
                              %mo (
                              %msup
                                %mo ∫
                                %mrow
                                  %mi c
                                  %mo ∈
                                  %mi 𝒞
                              %mi y
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi c
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo ⋅
                              %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                %mi X
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi c
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo )
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≔
                            %msup
                              %mo ∫
                              %mrow
                                %mi c
                                %mo ∈
                                %mi 𝒞
                            %mi F
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi c
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ⋅
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi c
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi 𝒟
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{aligned}
                    \\widetilde F(\mathbf{X})
                    \&amp; =
                    \\widetilde F
                    \\left(
                    \\int^{c \in \mathcal{C}} y(c) \cdot \mathbf{X}(c)
                    \\right)
                    \&amp; \coloneqq
                    \\int^{c \in \mathcal{C}} F(c) \cdot \mathbf{X}(c)
                    \\;\;\;\;\in \mathcal{D}
                    \\end{aligned}
            %p
              (where the colimit (a
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coend"} coend
              = succeed "!)." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒟
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{D}
          %h2#free_cocompletion_of_large_categories Free cocompletion of large categories
          %p
            In general, given a locally small (but possibly large) category
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒜
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{A}
            %em small presheaves
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒜
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{A}
            as the full subcategory of the functor category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Fun
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝒜
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} op
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Set
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Fun(\mathcal{A}^{\mathrm{op}},\operatorname{Set})
            spanned by those functors that are colimits of small diagrams of representables. Equivalently, a
            %em small presheaf
            is a functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝒜
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} op
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F:\mathcal{A}^{\mathrm{op}} \to \operatorname{Set}
            such that there exists a functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi γ
                  %mo :
                  %mi 𝒞
                  %mo →
                  %mi 𝒜
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gamma:\mathcal{C} \to \mathcal{A}
            with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            small and a presheaf
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo ′
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} op
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F': \mathcal{C}^{\mathrm{op}}\to \operatorname{Set}
            such that
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Lan
                    %mi γ
                  %mi F
                  %mo ′
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F=\operatorname{Lan}_{\gamma} F'.
          %p
            This process of free cocompletion defines a functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            from the 2-category
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi CAT
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi locally
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi small
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi categories
                  %mo ,
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi functors
                  %mo ,
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi natural
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi transformations
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CAT = [locally \; small \; categories, \; functors, \; natural \; transformations ]
          %p to the 2-category
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Cocomp
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi locally
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi small
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi cocomplete
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi categories
                  %mo ,
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi cocontinuous
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi functors
                  %mo ,
                  %mi natural
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi transformations
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cocomp = [locally \; small \; cocomplete \; categories, \; cocontinuous \; functors, natural \; transformations ]
          %p
            where, just to be clear, ‘cocomplete’ means having all
            %em small
            colimits, as usual. Moreover, this functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            is part of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pseudoadjunction"} pseudoadjunction
            where the right adjoint
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                  %mo :
                  %mi Cocomp
                  %mo →
                  %mi CAT
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R: Cocomp \to CAT
            assigns each locally small coccomplete category its underlying category, and so on.
          %p
            In the case where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝒜
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} op
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{A}^{\mathrm{op}}
            is
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+presentable"} locally presentable
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒜
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{A}
            is equivalent to the category of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/accessible+functors"} accessible functors
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝒜
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} op
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{A}^{\mathrm{op}}\to \operatorname{Set}
            = succeed "." do
              %em almost a topos
          %p
            See
            %a{:href => "#DayLack"} Day-Lack
            for more details on all these matters. They handle the more general case of enriched categories.
          %h2#free_cocompletion_as_a_pseudomonad Free cocompletion as a pseudomonad
          %p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Corfield"}> David Corfield
            \: So is this ‘free cocompletion’ part of an adjunction between the category of categories and the category of cocomplete categories (modulo size worries?). Or should we think of it as part of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pseudoadjunction"} pseudoadjunction
            between
            = succeed "?" do
              %em 2-categories
          %p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Baez"}> John Baez
            \: Equations between functors tends to hold only up to natural isomorphism. So, your first guess should not be that there’s an
            %em adjunction
            between the
            %em categories
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi CAT
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CAT
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Cocomp
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cocomp
            %em pseudoadjunction
            between the
            %em 2-categories
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi CAT
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CAT
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Cocomp
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cocomp
          %p This means there’s a forgetful 2-functor:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                  %mo :
                  %mi Cocomp
                  %mo →
                  %mi CAT
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R: Cocomp \to CAT
          %p together with a ‘free cocompletion’ 2-functor:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                  %mo :
                  %mi CAT
                  %mo →
                  %mi Cocomp
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L: CAT \to Cocomp
          %p And, it mean there’s an equivalence of categories
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi hom
                    %mi Cocomp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi F
                  %mi C
                  %mo ,
                  %mi D
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %msub
                    %mi hom
                    %mi CAT
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo ,
                  %mi U
                  %mi D
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  hom_{Cocomp} (F C, D) \simeq
                  hom_{CAT} (C, U D)
          %p
            for every
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi CAT
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C \in CAT
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Cocomp
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D \in Cocomp
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pseudonatural+transformation"} pseudonatural
            as a function of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
          %p If we have a pseudonatural equivalence of categories
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi hom
                    %mi Cocomp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi F
                  %mi C
                  %mo ,
                  %mi D
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %msub
                    %mi hom
                    %mi CAT
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo ,
                  %mi U
                  %mi D
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  hom_{Cocomp} (F C, D) \simeq
                  hom_{CAT} (C, U D)
          %p instead of a natural isomorphism of sets, then we say we have a ‘pseudoadjunction’ instead of an adjunction. A pseudoadjunction is the right generalization of adjunction when we go to 2-categories; if we were feeling in a modern mood we might just say ‘adjunction’ and expect people to know we meant ‘pseudo’.
          %p
            The details have been worked out by
            %a{:href => "#DayLack"} Day-Lack
            in even more generality: they consider enriched categories. Note that the free cocompletion of a
            %em small
            category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is the category of all presheaves on
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %em locally small
            category it’s just the category of small presheaves.
          %p
            In
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "http://www.lacim.uqam.ca/~gambino/species.pdf"} their work on species
            %em do
            use the
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi C
                    %mo ^
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widehat{C}
            construction all over the place. Somehow they’ve managed to avoid the need to consider this construction as a pseudomonad!
          %p
            Fiore, Gambino, Hyland and Winskel later exhibited the free cocompletion of a small category as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relative+pseudomonad"} relative pseudomonad
            from the 2-category Cat of small categories into the 2-category CAT of locally-small categories (via the 2-category COC of locally-small cocomplete categories). See
            %a{:href => "#FGHW"} FGHW
            for more details.
          %h2#in_higher_category_theory In higher category theory
          %p
            One can ask for the notion of free cocompletion in the wider context of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+category+theory"} higher category theory
          %ul
            %li
              for
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
              theory there is
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-cocompletion"} free (∞,1)-cocompletion
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p free cocompletions
              %ul
                %li
                  %p
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+strict+cocompletion"} free strict cocompletion
                %li
                  %p
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+coproduct+completion"} free coproduct completion
                %li
                  %p
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/idempotent+completion"}> idempotent completion
                    ,
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Karoubi+envelope"} Karoubi envelope
                %li
                  %p
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cauchy+completion"} Cauchy completion
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+completion"} free completion
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+bicompletion"} free bicompletion
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conservative+cocompletion"} conservative cocompletion
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ind-object"} ind-object
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sind-object"} sind-object
          %h2#references References
          %ul
            %li#DayLack
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Brian+Day"}> Brian Day
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Steve+Lack"} Steve Lack
                %em Limits of small functors
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0610439"}> web
                )
            %li#FGHW
              %p
                Fiore, Gambino, Hyland and Winskel,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Relative pseudomonads, Kleisli bicategories, and substitution monoidal structures
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/pdf/1612.03678.pdf"} web
            %li#PT
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paolo+Perrone"}> Paolo Perrone
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Walter+Tholen"} Walter Tholen
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Kan extensions are partial colimits
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2101.04531"} arXiv:2101.04531
          %p
            On
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+free+cocompletions"} strict free cocompletions
          %ul
            %li
              Erwan Beurier, Dominique Pastor, and René Guitart.
              = succeed "." do
                %em Presentations of clusters and strict free-cocompletions
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Theory+and+Applications+of+Categories"} Theory and Applications of Categories
              36.17 (2021): 492-513. (
              %a{:href => "http://www.tac.mta.ca/tac/volumes/36/17/36-17abs.html"}> link
              )
          %p This reference might also give helpful clues:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Dugger"}> Daniel Dugger
              ,
              %em Sheaves and Homotopy Theory
              (
              %a{:href => "http://www.uoregon.edu/~ddugger/cech.html"}> web
              ,
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/cech.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            A pedagogical explanation of the universal property of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+embedding"} Yoneda embedding
            is given starting on page 7. On page 8 there’s an explanation with lots of pictures how a presheaf is an “instruction for how to build a colimit”. Then on p. 9 the universal morphism that we are looking for here is identified as the one that “takes the instructions for building a colimit and actually
            %em builds
            it”.
          %p (This text, by the way, contains various other gems. A pity that it is left unfinished.)
          %p An early paper on free completions:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/V%C4%9Bra+Trnkov%C3%A1"}> Věra Trnková
              \.
              = succeed "," do
                %em Limits in categories and limit-preserving functors
        .revisedby
